===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|daddy-longlegs}}, {{l|en|daddy-long-legs}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|daddy}} + {{m|en|longlegs}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈdædɪ ˈlɒŋ(ɡ)leɡz/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[daddy]] [[long]][[legs]]|daddy longlegs|daddy longlegses}}

# {{lb|en|UK|Ireland}} The [[cranefly]]; any insect of the suborder [[Tipulomorpha]].
#* {{quote-text|year=2004|author=Bill Hansford-Steele|title=African Fly-fishing Handbook|page=316|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=XwPJJO4vOJkC&pg=PA316&dq=%22daddy+longlegs%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=Fi81T8faCMqViQfz29WjAg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22daddy%20longlegs%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|passage='''Daddy longlegs''' adults are weak flyers, falling onto the water surface in the lightest of breezes, and even on calm days.}}
# {{lb|en|Australia|Canada|New Zealand|US}} Any (non-spider) [[arachnid]] of the order [[Opiliones]], mostly with long [[thin]] [[leg]]s; the [[harvestman]].
#* '''2002''', Maurice Burton, Robert Burton, ''The International Wildlife Encyclopedia'', Volume 10, [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=ojMQP6aWW6sC&pg=PA636&dq=%22daddy+longlegs%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=Ews1T6nhOu3vmAWhhO33AQ&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22daddy%20longlegs%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false page 636],
#*: ''Unlike spiders, '''daddy longlegs''' do not have a clearly marked division between thorax and abdomen. They are further distinguished from spiders in that they do not produce venom or silk.''
#* '''2004''', Clay Thompson, Marshall Trimble, ''The Valley 101 Great Big Book of Life'', [http://books.google.com.au/books?id=FUgKx6oIV00C&pg=PA33&dq=%22daddy+longlegs%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=1iQ1T-COLsnDmQX-1_WNAg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22daddy%20longlegs%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false page 33],
#*: '''Daddy longlegs''' aren′t even really spiders.
# {{lb|en|loosely}} The [[daddy long-legs spider]], any spider of the family [[Pholcidae]].
#* {{quote-text|year=2010|author=Lou Bensinger|title=Tiny Invaders in Your Home|page=10|url=http://books.google.com.au/books?id=jAAZ0BLY8xUC&pg=PA10&dq=%22daddy+longlegs%22+-intitle:%22%22+-inauthor:%22%22&hl=en&sa=X&ei=fyc1T5n4JYTGmQXf2bibAg&redir_esc=y#v=onepage&q=%22daddy%20longlegs%22%20-intitle%3A%22%22%20-inauthor%3A%22%22&f=false|passage=Another spider neighbor that is commonly found in homes is the '''daddy longlegs'''. The '''daddy longlegs''' is often called a cellar spider.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|insect of suborder Tipulomorpha}} {{l|en|cranefly}}, {{l|en|tipulid}}
* {{sense|arachnid of order Opiliones}} {{l|en|harvestman}}
* {{sense|spider of family Pholcidae}} [[cellar spider]]

====Usage notes====
Some confusion exists because of the use of (almost) the same term for an insect, a non-spider arachnid and a spider. This is partly alleviated by some authors by reserving the term {{m|en|daddy long-legs spider}} for the spider alone.

